WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.100
I'm sort of starting to hope very, very cautiously
that American farmers are

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.019
realizing that Donald Trump is the reason
that a lot of these new struggles they're

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:15.259
experiencing are part of their reality and
hopefully they're going to hold them accountable

00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:19.430
for that in 2020 particularly because a lot
of those Midwest states in which these farmers

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:23.970
were side, we're very close in 2016 and could
make the difference between Donald Trump being

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:28.030
reelected or not being reelected. As you may
know, the White House has been running up

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:32.489
these huge deficits with their tax cut for
the rich. They've also been running up deficits

00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:38.170
a with subsidies to farmers to make up for
the crushing consequences of Donald Trump's

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:42.399
tariffs, and the White House has now announced
that they're going to add an additional billion

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:47.629
dollars to help out farmers, but the bailout
of the farmers does not actually solve the

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:53.289
underlying issue, which is that the tariffs
that Donald Trump has put in place have decimated

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:56.739
the markets in which these farmers operate.

00:00:56.739 --> 00:01:02.120
Soybean farmers are being destroyed in the
u s China's going to Brazil for soybeans instead

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.710
of coming here. That's great for China. It's
great for Brazilian farmers. It's terrible

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:11.870
for American farmers and for our own economy.
Since our farmers have less money that they

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:18.780
can then spend within the United States. When,
uh, the wheat farmers started to be destroyed

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:24.390
as a result of Trump's tariffs, China started
going to Russian regions for wheat. It's fine

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:30.751
for China, certainly welcomed by Russian farmers.
It's not so great for the United States. So

00:01:30.751 --> 00:01:37.000
we're finally starting to hear from farmers
that they're recognizing that this is a direct

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.950
result of Donald Trump's trade policy, that
this is the trade war. And remember, Trump

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:47.670
ran on, he understands trade better than anyone.
He's going to fix trade and none of it has

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.840
happened. The question then becomes, if they
realize that the farmers that is, will they

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.800
hold Trump accountable in 2020 I have no idea,
but I hope so.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.230
But it's important to understand that just
because you don't like Trump's trade policy

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:05.000
or recognize that it's been hurting you, it
doesn't necessarily mean you're going to vote

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.619
for a Democrat if you're a Midwestern republican
farmer. Now, there's also another winner from

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:14.121
this trade war, and this is not being discussed
that much and I think it's important. These

00:02:14.121 --> 00:02:23.189
tariffs are a handout too. American big farming
or big agribusiness in that as the small farmers

00:02:23.189 --> 00:02:28.230
struggle to make ends meet, they have much
less of an ability to weather unstable revenue

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:32.999
than do the big agribusiness companies. A
lot of those small farmers will start to think,

00:02:32.999 --> 00:02:38.390
damn, maybe I should get out of this business.
I wonder if I could maybe sell out altogether.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:42.950
Maybe some huge agribusiness conglomerate
will buy me out at a significant discount

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:48.280
because I'm struggling so badly, which has
the effect of further consolidating the food

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:54.930
production of the United States among few
very large factory farmers and multinational

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.670
agribusiness type companies.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:02.250
So make no mistake if you're a farmer and
you voted for Trump, this is what you voted

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:06.739
for in the sense that Trump promised it. He
pretended to have a clue about tariffs and

00:03:06.739 --> 00:03:11.590
trade. He clearly convinced enough people
that he has a clue on that to get them to

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:17.590
vote for him. And he did what he promised
to do. It's a disaster. And anyone who understood

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.639
what Trump was planning to do than you, it
would be a disaster all along. They did do

00:03:21.639 --> 00:03:26.890
it to themselves, those farmers. But I still
feel for them, I guess I see them as adults

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:32.569
who decide things for themselves, except they
have a disease of sorts called hyper partisanship.

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:37.069
Like in the same way that you wouldn't get
mad at someone for being an alcoholic because

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:40.700
it's sort of like getting mad at someone for
being a diabetic.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:47.250
Uh, we have all of us to some degree have
this partisanship that blinds us in some way,

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:53.090
shape or form. You become addicted to political
party. You become drunk off of disinformation

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:57.760
and political attack ads and talking points.
And then you end up voting for Donald Trump

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:03.319
and destroying your own business by virtue
of the policies that you vote in. Vote by

00:04:03.319 --> 00:04:08.099
voting for Donald Trump in the first place.
And that's why sadly, many of these farmers

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:14.469
are going to vote for Donald Trump again cause
they ain't voting for no Democrat, Sissy Liberal.

00:04:14.469 --> 00:04:21.590
They decided, I guess that a businessman with
a track record of bankruptcy, of not paying

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:27.320
vendors and employing undocumented immigrants
and scamming people was the guy to lead them

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:32.060
forward and now this is what they get, but
you know what? I still want to help them out

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:37.810
and I'll be doing it at least partially, partially
by working to remove Donald Trump in 2020

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:42.410
even if a lot of these farmers are going to
vote for their continued self-destruction

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:47.520
by voting to reelect Donald Trump in 2020
and many of them sadly will. Hopefully enough

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:52.570
of them realize not only is this Trump's fault,
but I should vote for someone else in November

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:58.220
of 2020 that he will lose some of those Midwestern
states that he won in 2016 way too early to

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:28.539
know, but obviously we will eventually figure

00:05:28.539 --> 00:06:14.550
that out.

